# Godot 4
.godot/
.import/
export.cfg
export_presets.cfg
*.translation

# TrenchBroom editor autosave backups (the committed source is maps/<name>.map)
maps/autosave/
# CYBER SUNDAY content-editor recoverable-save backups (ContentSaveGuard writes <name>.tres.bak on overwrite —
# a throwaway local one-deep undo, never committed content).
*.tres.bak
# GDExtension hot-reload temps (Windows copies the live .dll to a ~-prefixed name)
~*.dll

# Mono / C# (if added later)
.mono/
mono_crash.*.json

# Editors / OS
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.tmp
*.swp
*.bak
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# The dog's source art (assets/models/weirdlittleclayguy.obj, assets/models/dogcrate/*,
# assets/audio/sfx/aww.mp3) used to be ignored here while the mesh was 432 MB. It was slimmed to 14 MB and has
# been TRACKED since 2026-09-10 (the .obj through LFS — see .gitattributes), because scenes/characters/dog.tscn
# and scenes/props/dogcrate.tscn are live and a clone without them fails four content tests in CI.
# Do not re-ignore them. `dogcrate_Material Base Color.png` keeps its non-snake_case name on purpose:
# dogcrate.glb embeds that texture and imports with gltf/embedded_image_handling=1 (Extract Textures), so Godot
# re-extracts it under that exact name on every reimport; renaming it just leaves a stale orphan.
